          {
            title: 'President',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'President is a card game card game that involves gameplay, scoring, strategy. The game originated in Various and has become popular worldwide.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Probably China; immediate ancestor the Japanese game Dai Hin Min (Daifugō). Westernized and spread throughout the Western world (USA, Britain, Australia, France, Germany, Hungary, Denmark, Netherlands) by end of 20th century.\nTime Period: Known in the West since the 1970s; climbing games long established in China.\nHistorical Development: Evolved from Chinese climbing games (e.g. Zheng Shangyou); Japanese Dai Hin Min is the direct ancestor; spread as a shedding game among young people.\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game in many countries under names such as Scum, Asshole, Trouduc, Hübéres.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nScore sheet (optional)\nTable space',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards per Player: Varies by player count\nDealing Pattern: Clockwise\n--',
              },
            ],
          },
